      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Methods in Queue\n------------------------------------------\n\n1. For adding data\n-------------------------\n\n a.  add ( ) : accepts an element and add it to the Queue .\nIf unable to add the element it throws an Exception called\nIllegalStateExcception . This happens when we use\nLinkedBoundedQueue which is a size restricted Queue , then\non overflow condition it throws exception .\n\n\n b.  offer ( ) : accepts an element and add it to the Queue .\nIf unable to add the element it reteurn false .\n\n\n\n\n2. For deleting data\n-----------------------------\n\n c.  remove ( ) :  It deletes the element at the head of the\nQueue and returns it .  If Queue is empty it throws\nNoSuchElementException .\n\n\n d. poll ( ) :  It deletes the element at the head of the\nQueue and returns it . If Queue is empty it returns null .\n\n\n\n\n3. For accessing data \n------------------------------\n\n e. element ( ) : It returns the HEAD element of the Queue .\nIf Queue is empty it throws NoSuchElementException .\n\n \n f. peek ( ) :  It returns the HEAD element of the Queue . If\nQueue is empty it returns null .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Methods in Queue\n------------------------------------------\n\n1. For adding data\n-------------------------\n\n a.  add ( ) : accepts an element and add it to the Queue . If unable to add the element it throws an Exception called IllegalStateExcception . This happens when we use LinkedBoundedQueue which is a size restricted Queue , then on overflow condition it throws exception .\n\n\n b.  offer ( ) : accepts an element and add it to the Queue . If unable to add the element it reteurn false .\n\n\n\n\n2. For deleting data\n-----------------------------\n\n c.  remove ( ) :  It deletes the element at the head of the Queue and returns it .  If Queue is empty it throws NoSuchElementException .\n\n\n d. poll ( ) :  It deletes the element at the head of the Queue and returns it . If Queue is empty it returns null .\n\n\n\n\n3. For accessing data \n------------------------------\n\n e. element ( ) : It returns the HEAD element of the Queue . If Queue is empty it throws NoSuchElementException .\n\n \n f. peek ( ) :  It returns the HEAD element of the Queue . If Queue is empty it returns null .",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
